<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
<!--
    Re-points the stock Invoice/Credit Note report onto
    sgc_report_theme_core.external_layout_sgc. Same pattern proven in
    sgc_report_theme_business/_statement/_sales: changes ONLY the t-call
    target attribute, no t-esc/t-field value expression touched anywhere.

    WHY THE HIDDEN ANCHOR
    ---------------------
    account_edi_ubl_cii (core Odoo 19, UAE e-invoicing) inherits
    account.report_invoice_document and rewrites the very same layout call
    with a LITERAL XPath:

        <xpath expr="//t[@t-call='web.external_layout']" position="attributes">

    Odoo combines inherited views with EXTENSIONS FIRST and primaries after
    (see ir_ui_view._combine), so this bridge - an extension - always runs
    BEFORE account_edi_ubl_cii's primary view. Once this bridge changes the
    t-call, the core module looks for a literal value that is no longer
    there and the whole registry load fails:

        Element '<xpath expr="//t[@t-call='web.external_layout']">' cannot
        be located in parent view

    That aborts the database initialisation - the site is down until
    somebody removes one of the two modules. It is not hypothetical:
    account_peppol auto-installs account_edi_ubl_cii, so installing
    account_peppol was enough to take the database down.

    The hidden anchor keeps a literal web.external_layout call reachable, so
    the core module always finds its target. It sits in a t-if="False"
    holder, so it renders nothing; it exists purely so the two rewrites
    cannot collide. The invoice PDF still carries the SGC theme, and the
    UAE e-invoice XML is unaffected either way - it is generated
    server-side by account_edi_xml_cii_facturx._export_invoice, not from
    this template.

    priority="99" applies this view last among the extensions, so any
    other module that rewrites the same call keeps working too.
-->

    <template id="report_invoice_document_sgc"
              inherit_id="account.report_invoice_document"
              priority="99">
        <xpath expr="//t[@t-call='web.external_layout']" position="attributes">
            <attribute name="t-call">sgc_report_theme_core.external_layout_sgc</attribute>
        </xpath>

        <xpath expr="//t[@t-call='sgc_report_theme_core.external_layout_sgc']" position="after">
            <t t-if="False"><t t-call="web.external_layout"/></t>
        </xpath>
    </template>

</odoo>
